# Update PROJECT_CONTEXT when you ship code

`PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` is the repo source of truth for what is **Shipped**, **Partial**, **Planned**, or **Not in repo**. When your edits under `src/` or `supabase/migrations/` **materially change** what users or advisors can do, you **must** update that file **in the same task** before finishing — do not leave it for the user.

After updating inventory, follow `.cursor/rules/project-context-notion-sync.mdc` to sync [BYOFA Features](https://www.notion.so/BYOFA-Features-35fa694147bf8093be2fc57673cee41a) unless the user said to skip Notion.

## Update PROJECT_CONTEXT when you

- Add or remove an **App Router** page, layout segment, or API route clients/advisors hit
- Add or change **middleware** gating, auth flows, onboarding, or shell navigation
- Ship or extend a **feature module** under `src/features/` (new UI surface, not just a refactor)
- Add a **migration** that introduces or changes user-visible tables/columns, RLS, or RPCs the app calls
- Change **advisor ↔ client** workflows (proposals, access keys, roster, contact)
- Flip a capability from placeholder/scaffold to working (or the reverse)

## Do not update for

- Pure refactors, renames, or internal moves with **no** behavior change
- Tests, stories, comments, or tooling only
- Style, copy tweaks, or bugfixes that do not change shipped vs planned scope
- Domain math tweaks that do not change which modules exist

## What to edit in PROJECT_CONTEXT.md

1. **[Feature inventory (shipped vs planned)]** — add/update/remove the capability row: **Status** + concise **Notes** (routes, key files, migrations). Use factual wiring, not marketing.
2. **Routes** and/or **Database** — one or two bullets when a new route, table, or RPC matters.
3. **Code map** — only for a new top-level domain area.
4. **`_Last reviewed_`** line at the bottom — one sentence on what changed.

Status meanings: **Shipped** = end-to-end for normal users; **Partial** = real workflow plus known gaps; **Planned** = placeholder/card only; **Not in repo** = not implemented.

## Notion row mapping

When adding inventory rows, use product **Feature** titles from `.cursor/rules/project-context-notion-sync.mdc` so BYOFA stays aligned (e.g. split Home metrics into dashboard / net worth / spending rows when appropriate).

## Completion check

Before you mark the task done, confirm either:

- PROJECT_CONTEXT was updated (list which inventory rows changed), **or**
- You explicitly state why this change did not warrant an update (e.g. internal refactor only).
